{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1553782851,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MjY1MTk0ODg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3276","origin":"github"},"title":"Unify interface for \"entity\" based operations?","message":"May be there is already an issue - didn't find it upon quick search.  But I bet we already discussed it at least in the context of `create-sibling` vs `siblings create`.  So ATM we have\n- `subdatasets`\n\nBUT for other entities we do not have similar \"gate\" command with sub-actions, while by default just listing the known entities of the kind.  E.g. we have following commands which list different entities\n- `containters-list` (from `datalad-container` extension)\n- `run-procedure --discover` - to list procedures\n- `search --show-keys` - a bit of a stretch here, and if any RF might just need to migrate somehow into `metadata` command probably?\n\nSo I wonder if we should look into unifying interface across those, so whenever there is a clear entity which commands operate \"on\" (`containers`, `procedures`) - there should be a gateway command which would by default just list the known ones (like `siblings` and `subdatasets` do now)","files":null}]}